   "id": "formalization-routes",
   "title": "Five formulations of Poisson's equation",
   "caption": "For \\(-\\Delta u=f\\), take a bounded smooth domain \\(\\Omega\\) and continuous \\(f\\) on its closure. A locally integrable distributional solution tests against \\(\\varphi\\in C_c^\\infty(\\Omega)\\). If also \\(u\\in H^1(\\Omega)\\), density extends the identity to every \\(v\\in H_0^1(\\Omega)\\). On a fixed trace class, the weak equation is the first-variation condition for the convex energy \\(E(u)=\\tfrac12\\int_\\Omega|\\nabla u|^2-\\int_\\Omega fu\\), hence is equivalent to minimizing it. Viscosity solutions use smooth functions touching \\(u\\) from above and below. The dashed arrows need the labelled regularity; weak solvability alone does not give \\(C^2\\). The separate semigroup box concerns evolution \\(u_t=Au\\). PDEAtlas develops semigroup tools as well as weak evolution on Gelfand triples.",
   "alt": "Five connected boxes for classical, distributional, viscosity, weak and variational Poisson solutions. Classical implies distributional by integration by parts; the reverse weak-to-classical arrow requires regularity. The distributional-to-weak arrow requires H¹ membership. Weak and variational solutions agree for the displayed convex energy with fixed trace. An unconnected box shows the separate semigroup evolution formula u(t)=S(t)u₀.",
