   "caption": "Both problems start from \\(g(x)=1/(1+x^2)\\), analytic on the whole line. Left: the wave equation with \\(u_t(0,x)=0\\). At \\(x=0\\) the partial sums \\(S_N(t)=\\sum_{k\\le N}(-1)^kt^{2k}\\) for \\(N=1,2,5,6,15,16\\) approach the exact value \\(1/(1+t^2)\\) for \\(t<1\\). At the dashed line \\(t=1\\) they alternate between \\(0\\) and \\(1\\), and beyond it they separate, odd \\(N\\) downward and even \\(N\\) upward. Right: the heat equation. The \\(k\\)-th term of its formal series at \\(x=0\\) has size \\((2k)!\\,t^k/k!\\), plotted on a base-ten logarithmic scale for three times. Each sequence falls until \\(k\\) is about \\(1/(4t)\\) and then grows without bound, crossing the dashed line of terms of size one, so the series diverges at every \\(t>0\\).",
