   "caption": "Left: a bounded planar domain \\(\\Omega\\) with smooth boundary, outward unit normals \\(\\nu\\) at twelve boundary points, and the field \\(F(x,y)=(x+0.4y,\\,0.3x^2)\\) at the same points. Here \\(\\operatorname{div}F=1\\), so \\(\\int_\\Omega\\operatorname{div}F\\) is the area of \\(\\Omega\\), and the computed flux \\(\\int_{\\partial\\Omega}F\\cdot\\nu\\,d\\sigma\\) agrees with it to six decimals. Right: near a boundary point the domain is the region above a \\(C^1\\) graph \\(x_n=\\gamma(x')\\). The outward normal is \\((\\nabla\\gamma,-1)/\\sqrt{1+|\\nabla\\gamma|^2}\\), pointing below the graph, and a parameter interval of length \\(dy\\) carries boundary length \\(\\sqrt{1+|\\nabla\\gamma|^2}\\,dy\\).",
