   "id": "heaviside-dirac",
   "title": "Smoothing the Heaviside function",
   "caption": "The Heaviside function \\(H\\) convolved with the mollifier \\(\\eta_\\varepsilon\\) is the smooth step \\(H_\\varepsilon=H*\\eta_\\varepsilon\\), and its classical derivative is \\(\\eta_\\varepsilon\\) itself. The animation steps through seven computed values of \\(\\varepsilon\\) from \\(0.8\\) to \\(0.1\\). Left: \\(H_\\varepsilon\\) against the step \\(H\\). Right: \\(\\eta_\\varepsilon\\), whose peak leaves the panel at small \\(\\varepsilon\\), together with a fixed test function \\(\\varphi\\). The printed pairing \\(\\int\\eta_\\varepsilon\\varphi\\), computed both directly and as \\(-\\int H_\\varepsilon\\varphi'\\), approaches \\(\\varphi(0)\\), which is the value of \\(\\delta_0\\) on \\(\\varphi\\).",
   "alt": "Two panels. Left, a smooth S-shaped curve that steepens toward a dashed unit step at the origin. Right, a narrowing bump centred at the origin beside a wider fixed bump centred slightly to the right, with a line of text giving the current value of the pairing next to the value of the wide bump at zero.",
