   "caption": "On \\((-1,1)\\), \\(u(x)=|x|\\) has weak derivative \\(\\operatorname{sgn}(x)\\). The dashed test is \\(\\varphi(x)=b((x-0.2)/0.7)\\), supported on \\([-0.5,0.9]\\), where \\(b(z)=\\exp(1-1/(1-z^2))\\) for \\(|z|<1\\), zero outside. Below, the signed areas of \\(|x|\\varphi'\\) and \\(-\\operatorname{sgn}(x)\\varphi\\) agree numerically, both approximately \\(-0.389\\). Integration by parts on each side of zero proves the identity for every smooth compactly supported test: outer boundary terms vanish with \\(\\varphi\\), and terms at zero vanish with \\(|x|\\). Changing \\(\\operatorname{sgn}(0)\\) affects neither integral. Agreement for the plotted test illustrates this argument; it does not establish a weak derivative by itself.",
