   "title": "Extension across a flat boundary by reflection",
   "caption": "A function \\(u(t)=0.6+0.5\\sin(2.2t)\\) on \\((0,1)\\) and two ways to continue it to \\((-1,1)\\). Left: the even reflection \\(Eu(t)=u(|t|)\\) meets \\(u\\) at \\(t=0\\) with the same value, while the zero extension (dashed) jumps by \\(u(0)=0.6\\). Right: the derivatives. \\((Eu)'\\) is the odd reflection of \\(u'\\); it jumps at zero but is still square integrable, so \\(Eu\\in H^1(-1,1)\\). The derivative of the zero extension contains the point mass \\(0.6\\,\\delta_0\\), drawn as an arrow, and is not a function. Each integral in the graph norm doubles: numerically \\(\\|Eu\\|_{H^1(-1,1)}^2=2.839=2\\times1.419\\).",
