   "caption": "The function \\(u(x,t)=e^{-(x-1.2t)^2-t}\\) on the half-plane \\(t>0\\). Left: level curves of \\(u\\) and the strip \\(0<t<\\varepsilon\\). Right: the restriction \\(u(x,0)=e^{-x^2}\\) (dashed) and the strip average \\(A_\\varepsilon u(x)=\\varepsilon^{-1}\\int_0^\\varepsilon u(x,t)\\,dt\\) for \\(\\varepsilon=0.8,0.4,0.2,0.1,0.05\\), all drawn faintly, with one highlighted at a time. The average reads \\(u\\) only inside the half-plane. The labels give the computed \\(L^2\\) distance to the restriction and the bound \\(\\varepsilon^{1/2}\\|\\partial_tu\\|_{L^2}\\) from the height-average theorem at \\(p=2\\). The static frame shows \\(\\varepsilon=0.8\\).",
   "alt": "Left, a half-plane with t upward and x across, closed level curves of a bump that drifts to the right as t grows, and a shaded strip along the boundary. Right, a dashed Gaussian and five fainter curves below it that approach it as the strip gets thinner; one of them is highlighted, with its strip width, its distance to the Gaussian and the theoretical bound.",
