   "id": "difference-quotient-limit",
   "title": "Difference quotients of a corner and of a jump",
   "caption": "The forward quotient \\(D^hu(x)=(u(x+h)-u(x))/h\\) for \\(h=0.5,0.3,0.2,0.125\\), all drawn faintly with one highlighted at a time. Left: the tent \\(u=\\max(0,1-|x|)\\), whose weak derivative (dashed) is \\(\\pm1\\). The quotients are ramps of width \\(h\\) around each corner and converge in \\(L^2\\), with \\(\\|D^hu-u'\\|_2=(2h)^{1/2}\\). Right: the jump \\(u=\\mathbf 1_{(0,1)}\\). The quotient is \\(1/h\\) on \\((-h,0]\\) and \\(-1/h\\) on \\([1-h,1)\\), so \\(\\|D^hu\\|_2=(2/h)^{1/2}\\) is unbounded as \\(h\\to0\\), while \\(\\|D^hu\\|_1=2\\) for every \\(h\\).",
   "alt": "Two panels. Left, a dashed step function equal to one on minus one to zero and minus one on zero to one, with trapezoid-shaped quotient curves whose ramps narrow towards the step. Right, two rectangular spikes, up just left of zero and down just left of one, that grow taller and narrower as h shrinks.",
