   "caption": "Left: level curves of \\(G(x,\\cdot)\\) for the unit disc and the pole \\(x=(0.5,0.2)\\). The corrector is the fundamental solution centred at the reflected point \\(x^*=x/|x|^2\\), scaled by \\(|x|\\), so the difference vanishes on the circle; outside the disc the same formula continues with its second pole at \\(x^*\\), drawn dashed. The generator checks \\(G=0\\) on the circle and \\(G(x,y)=G(y,x)\\) on 1521 pairs. Right: the Poisson kernel \\(K(x,\\zeta)=-\\partial_\\nu G(x,\\zeta)\\) as a function of the angle between \\(\\zeta\\) and \\(x\\), for \\(|x|=0,0.4,0.6,0.75\\). Each has mass one, checked by quadrature, and it concentrates at the angle \\(0\\) as \\(x\\) approaches the boundary, which is why the Poisson integral takes the boundary values.",
   "alt": "A disc containing nested closed curves around an interior point, with a dashed line through the centre and the point to a second point outside the disc, where dashed curves circle it; beside it, four bell-shaped curves over an angle axis, each taller and narrower than the last.",
