   "id": "hopf-lemma",
   "title": "Hopf's lemma: a strict boundary maximum has a nonzero normal slope",
   "caption": "Left: the harmonic function \\(u=\\operatorname{Re}(z-0.2z^2)\\) on the unit disc attains its maximum \\(0.8\\) only at \\(x_0=(1,0)\\). The shaded annulus \\(\\tfrac12<|x|<1\\) is the only region where the Lean statement asks for ellipticity, coefficient bounds and \\(Lu\\le 0\\). Right: along the radius ending at \\(x_0\\), the gap \\(u(x_0)-u\\) stays above \\(\\varepsilon v\\), where \\(v=e^{-5|x|^2}-e^{-5}\\) vanishes on the circle and \\(\\Delta v>0\\) on the annulus. The constant \\(\\varepsilon\\approx1.251\\) is the smallest gap on the inner circle divided by \\(v\\) there, and the inequality is checked on a polar grid of the annulus. Both curves vanish at \\(x_0\\), so the slope of the gap is at least the slope of \\(\\varepsilon v\\), which is \\(0.084\\); the actual normal derivative is \\(0.6\\). The dotted profile vanishes to second order at \\(x_0\\) and crosses below the barrier at \\(|x|=0.8\\), which is what the lemma rules out.",
