   "id": "harnack-disc",
   "title": "Positive harmonic functions on the disc cannot vary too fast inside",
   "caption": "Left: level curves of the Poisson kernel \\(P(x,\\zeta)=(1-|x|^2)/|x-\\zeta|^2\\) for \\(\\zeta=(1,0)\\). They are circles tangent to the boundary at \\(\\zeta\\). Right: \\(u(x)/u(0)\\) along the segment from \\(0\\) to \\(\\zeta\\), on a logarithmic scale, for the kernels with poles at angles \\(0,\\pi/4,\\pi/2,3\\pi/4,\\pi\\). Every one stays in the shaded band \\((1-r)/(1+r)\\le u/u(0)\\le(1+r)/(1-r)\\), whose edges are the kernels with poles at \\(0\\) and \\(\\pi\\); the inequality is checked on a grid of 181 poles. Positive harmonic functions on the disc are averages of these kernels, so they all obey the same bound. On the dashed disc \\(|x|\\le\\tfrac12\\) this gives \\(\\sup u\\le 9\\inf u\\). The Lean theorem proves that some such constant exists on any compact subset, by chaining balls, without computing the sharp value.",
   "alt": "A disc with a family of circles tangent at one boundary point and a smaller dashed disc inside; beside it, on a logarithmic vertical axis, five curves fanning out from the value one at the origin, all inside a shaded band whose edges are two of the curves.",
