  {
   "id": "moving-planes",
   "title": "Moving planes: the reflected cap stays above the solution",
   "caption": "The positive solution \\(u(x)=J_0(j_0|x|)\\) of \\(-\\Delta u=j_0^2u\\) on the unit disc, with \\(u=0\\) on the circle, where \\(j_0\\approx2.405\\) is the first zero of \\(J_0\\). Left: the plane \\(x_1=\\lambda\\), the cap \\(\\Sigma_\\lambda=\\{x\\in B: x_1>\\lambda\\}\\) shaded, and its mirror image, dashed, which stays inside the disc. Right: \\(u\\) along the \\(x_1\\)-axis and, over the cap, the reflected profile \\(u(2\\lambda-x_1,0)\\), dashed; the shaded gap is \\(w_\\lambda=u(x^\\lambda)-u\\ge0\\), checked on a grid of each cap. The static frame is \\(\\lambda=\\tfrac12\\); the animation moves the plane to \\(\\lambda=0\\), where the gap closes. The method starts with \\(\\lambda\\) near \\(1\\), where the boundary behaviour gives \\(w_\\lambda>0\\), and the strong maximum principle keeps \\(w_\\lambda>0\\) as long as \\(\\lambda>0\\). Running it from every direction makes \\(u\\) radial and strictly decreasing in \\(|x|\\).",
   "alt": "A disc with concentric level circles, a vertical line cutting off a shaded cap on the right, and a dashed mirror image of the cap on the other side of the line; beside it, a bell-shaped profile over an axis, a vertical line, and a dashed reflected profile above it on the right of the line with the gap shaded.",
