   "title": "The energy of heat flow is log-convex",
   "caption": "The solution \\(u=e^{-t}\\sin x+0.7e^{-9t}\\sin 3x+0.5e^{-49t}\\sin 7x\\) on \\((0,\\pi)\\) with zero boundary values. Left: \\(\\log E(t)\\) for \\(E(t)=\\int_0^\\pi u^2\\,dx\\), below its chord (dashed). The curve lies under the chord because \\((E')^2\\le EE''\\). Right: the frequency \\(\\int_0^\\pi u_x^2\\,dx\\big/\\int_0^\\pi u^2\\,dx=-E'/2E\\) decreases from a weighted average of \\(1,9,49\\) toward the lowest eigenvalue \\(1\\). Log-convexity gives \\(E(t)\\le E(0)^{1-t/b}E(b)^{t/b}\\) for \\(0\\le t\\le b\\), so \\(E(b)=0\\) forces \\(E=0\\) on \\([0,b]\\). That is backward uniqueness.",
