   "caption": "For \\(u_t+(u^2/2)_x=0\\), a characteristic carries \\(u_0(x_0)\\) along \\(x=x_0+t u_0(x_0)\\). These piecewise linear initial data have a downward ramp on \\([0,1]\\) and an upward jump at \\(x=2\\); they are not globally smooth. On the ramp \\(u_0'=-1\\), so characteristics meet at \\(t=1\\). The entropy solution continues with a downward jump from one to zero. Rankine–Hugoniot gives speed \\((1/2-0)/(1-0)=1/2\\), with characteristics entering the shock from both sides. The upward jump instead opens into \\(u=(x-2)/t\\) between \\(x=2\\) and \\(x=2+t\\). Every plotted time precedes the shock's encounter with the fan at \\(t=3\\). Compression creates a discontinuity while expansion fills a gap.",
