  {
   "id": "p-system-riemann-fan",
   "title": "A Riemann problem for the p-system",
   "caption": "The p-system \\(v_t-w_x=0\\), \\(w_t-p(v)_x=0\\) with \\(p(v)=e^v\\), so \\(c=e^{v/2}\\) and \\(A(v)=2e^{v/2}-2\\). The left state \\(u_L=(0,0)\\) is joined to \\(u_M\\) by a 0-rarefaction of strength \\(-0.8\\), along which \\(w-A(v)\\) is constant, and \\(u_M\\) to \\(u_R\\) by a 1-shock of strength \\(-1\\) on the Hugoniot curve. Left: the fan of 0-characteristics \\(x/t=-c(v)\\) and the shock \\(x=st\\), \\(s\\approx0.533\\). The thin curves are 1-characteristics, \\(dx/dt=c(v)\\): they bend in the fan, and the ones ahead of the shock are overtaken by it, the Lax condition \\(c(v_R)<s<c(v_M)\\). Right: the two wave curves in the state plane, the solid parts being the ones used. These explicit formulas are total; the Lean theorem concatenates the same elementary waves for states close together.",
   "alt": "Two panels. Left, the space-time plane with a fan of straight rays opening to the left of the origin, a thick straight shock line leaning right, and thin curves that bend through the fan or run into the shock from the right. Right, the state plane with a rarefaction curve from the left state down to a middle state and a shock curve from the middle state to the right state, both continued as thin curves beyond the parts used.",
