  {
   "id": "kovasznay-flow",
   "title": "A steady wake behind a row of obstacles",
   "caption": "Streamlines of Kovasznay's exact solution with \\(\\lambda=-1\\), \\(k=2\\) and \\(\\nu=1/3\\): \\(u=1-e^{-x}\\cos2y\\), \\(v=-\\tfrac12e^{-x}\\sin2y\\), \\(p=-\\tfrac12e^{-2x}\\). The three numbers satisfy \\(\\nu(\\lambda^2-k^2)=\\lambda\\), which is the whole condition for \\(e^{\\lambda x}\\) to balance convection against diffusion. The streamfunction is \\(\\psi=y-\\tfrac12e^{-x}\\sin2y\\), and the curves are its levels \\(\\pm0.1,\\pm0.3,\\dots,\\pm1.5\\). The pattern repeats with period \\(\\pi\\) in \\(y\\), and the lines \\(y=\\pm\\pi/2\\) are streamlines. In the shaded region \\(e^{-x}\\cos2y>1\\), so \\(u<0\\) and the fluid runs backwards. The boundary of that region is where streamlines turn vertical. The dot is the stagnation point at the origin. Far downstream the flow tends to the uniform stream \\(u=1\\); upstream it grows like \\(e^{-x}\\), so its energy on the plane is infinite.",
   "alt": "A rectangle in the plane with the flow entering from the left. Closed and open streamlines bend around a shaded lobe on the left, centred on the horizontal axis, where the horizontal velocity is negative. A dot marks the stagnation point at the origin. To the right the streamlines straighten into horizontal lines.",
