   "caption": "The error of four composite rules for \\(\\int_0^1e^x\\,dx=e-1\\) against the number of equal panels \\(N\\), both axes logarithmic. Marks are measured errors; each dashed line is the proved panel-rule bound \\(C(b-a)^{m+1}/(DN^m)\\) with \\(C=e\\). Left, order \\(m=2\\): \\(D=12\\) for the trapezoid rule and \\(D=24\\) for the midpoint rule. Right, order \\(m=4\\): \\(D=2880\\) for Simpson and \\(D=4320\\) for two-point Gauss-Legendre. The slopes are \\(-2\\) and \\(-4\\), and the marks sit a constant factor near \\((e-1)/e\\) below their bounds because \\(|f^{(m)}|=e^x\\) ranges from \\(1\\) to \\(e\\) while the bound uses its maximum.",
   "alt": "Two log-log panels with the number of panels from 1 to 32 on the horizontal axis. Left, the trapezoid and midpoint errors fall on parallel straight lines of slope minus two from about ten to the minus one to ten to the minus four. Right, the Simpson and two-point Gauss errors fall with slope minus four from about ten to the minus three to ten to the minus nine and a half. Each series lies just below a dashed bound line.",
